==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Mystic Egg: N004''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Supercar Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Supercar Cat is a glass cannon similar to [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Express Cat]], but as a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]]. It can do a Single Attack with high damage (nearly twice as much as an Express Cat with the same level, up to 81k at level 50) and knock a traited enemy back, with low range and frequency. However, comparing to Express Cat, it has extremely low survivability (negligible health, and will move forward right after attacking), even less range, slower rush speed and delayed attack, so it will usually land just one hit and must be timed extremely well (much harder than Express) to actually succeed. It excels in stages with little to no peons, or when used with a [[:Category:Waver-class Cats|Wave Attacker]] like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]] to destroy peons. [[Freshman Cat Jobs (Super Rare Cat)|Headmaster Cat Jobs]], units that can Freeze enemies for a long time, or a highly leveled [[Cat Cannon#Cannon Types|Thunderbolt Cannon]] synergize well with Supercar, as they can allow Supercar to hit an enemy it otherwise might not be able to, or even land an extra attack.

Supercar's knockback ability is useful for gaining ground against non-immune Traited enemies with low knockback counts and a long time between attacks/during attack animation, like [[Johnnyleon]], [[Zero Luza]] or [[Golem Sunfish]]. However, it is not as useful on enemies already with many damage-based knockbacks as you will be able to accomplish this with raw damage anyway.

Supercar works very well against most [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku Enemies]] thanks to its guaranteed chance to pierce [[Shield]]s, most notably [[Fallen Bear]]'s, [[High Priest Mamon]]'s, [[Ackey]]'s, [[Possessed Empress]]', and so on, since their attacks leave a small window of opportunity for it to destroy their shields. When it comes to breaking [[Barrier]]s, Supercar Cat, while not as useful due to the sheer abundance of superior alternatives, still comes in handy against certain enemies such as picking off [[UltraBaaBaa]]s or for rushing down [[Youcan]].

