==Trivia==
*Supercar Cat's "supercar" bears significant resemblance to a [https://jp.mercari.com/item/m61062943320 Japanese toy toilet].
**Supercar Cat's appearance and stats may also reference the [[mariowiki:Quacker|Quacker]] from ''[[mariowiki:Mario Kart Wii|Mario Kart Wii]]'', a duck-like bike that has great acceleration, handling, drift and mini-turbo but low mass that makes it incredibly easy to push around.
*This, [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N005]], and [[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N003]] are currently the only [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]] whose [[True Form]]s do not have Behemoth Slayer.
*[[Ancient Egg: N202 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N202]], [[Ancient Egg: N204 (Special Cat)|Ancient Egg: N204]] and Ancient Egg: N004 are currently the only [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]] whose Evolved and True Forms affect more than one trait with their abilities.
*Ironically, despite targeting traited enemies, Mystic Egg: N004 is white, suggesting it targets [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]].
*Supercar Cat is the only [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Egg]] who gains no health increase upon True Form, making the spammable egg forms as bulky as True Form.
*Tama-san, character designer and art director for [[The Battle Cats]], stated that Supercar Cat was an original character that he made to represent himself in company discussions. He was later surprised to see his own original character make it officially to the game<ref>https://x.com/tamasanp/status/1842429021679935701</ref>.
**Since Supercar Cat is an official character for the game, he is now using a different original character to represent himself during work.

